Well, I've finally done it! After playing this game for many years,
having resigned myself to the fact that I probably didn't have the
patience or 'temperament' to ascend, I've done it! I was so excited, I
called over my wife to observe the momentous occasion; she pretended to
be impressed (she thinks I might stop playing now - ha! - I've got to
ascend all the other classes first, then start on conducts - that's
another ten years right there).

I don't have too many details, as I started this particular game at
least a month ago, and have been playing it on and off since then. In
fact, I don't really remember the early game. I know I had a powerful
pet at one point, because I went back to minetown (to get candles) to
find several deserted shops, and I know I didn't do it. I seem to
remember a polymorph trap in the mines and a magic whistle changing
Brian the cat into Brian the baby dragon. I think he later stumbled
into another polymorph trap, and got turned back into something weak,
and got killed shortly after. I didn't pick up another pet for the rest
of the game.

I found a wand of wishing in the mines (a common theme for first
ascensions) after having got an amulet of reflection in sokoban, and
kitted myself up with GDSM, GoP, and speed boots. I established a base
near an altar on level 7, and dumped a load of stuff there. By the time
I'd accumulated some scrolls of identify to bless, I'd got a fair bit
of stuff, so I was pretty lucky that I got a full inventory identify on
first try. Sacrificing soon got me Mjollnir.

The quest was relatively easy, and I'd found a pair of levitation boots
by the time I got to Medusa. I'd also found the first of four amulets
of life saving (none of which ended up being used),  so I swapped that
out for the AoR, and wished for a shield of reflection instead.

By the time I got to Gehenomm, I was feeling like this could be it -
last time I got this far, I died in the Valley of the dead, so I was
into uncharted territory. I got a pleasant surprise at Juiblex's swamp
- hearse had got me the bones pile of some poor adventurer who'd had a
cockatrice mishap, and had left me a statue full of goodies. I got my
third wand of wishing (at 0:0, so still 4 wishes in it) and various
other nice things here - including many magic markers.

Shortly afterwards, I had an unfortunate encounter with a mind-flayer.
Well, he only sucked my brain once, so I didn't forget too much, but it
was irritating, none the less. I popped back up to my base, wrote some
genocide scrolls, and got rid of them as well as liches.

I was surprised at how easily defeated Juiblex and Baalzebub were, and
Asmodeus only wanted a little cash. I made it all the way to the fake
wizards towers with little difficulty, using the Orb of Fate every so
often to go back to my base and dump stuff. I also tried (for the first
ever time) polypiling, but only once, and, to be honest, got nothing
much better than I started with.

So, I carried on to the bottom of Gehenomm. And this is where I made a
mistake (although, clearly, it turned out to be non-fatal). I knew that
having the Amulet meant  increased hunger, etc, but I thought the
Wizard only reappeared when you had the Amulet. So, I thought "I'll
just kill the Rodney, then pop back up to my base, and sort out all my
stuff for the ascension run prior to getting the Amulet." I did this,
then got back, aand realised my inventory was all getting cursed and
the Wizard was reappearing. Oops! As a result of this, I realised it
was imperative to get moving, so I spent MUCH less time getting my
things ready for my ascension run than I intended.

Popped back down, and killed the high priest of Moloch with a rubber
chicken, grabbed the amulet, and ran for it. Damn, it was annoying
trying to get up. I must have hit Juiblex's swamp at least a dozen
times. Stopped briefly at my home level to pick up some more useful
stuff, then went for it.

The planes were less tough than I thought, except for water. I couldn't
find the portal, until I used the Orb of Fate to look for it, and then
stumbled into it more or less by accident. I realise in retrospect I
was also in danger of being drowned by eels, but none of them ever
seemed to hit me. (Note to self - next time, bring crystal ball if I
don't have Orb of Fate)

In the Astral plane, I was somewhat overwhelmed by the number of beings
out to get me. I guessed left (Pestilence) - wrong. tried centre
(Death) - wrong again. And suddenly I was burdened, and I noticed that
both my hands contained cursed items, and I couldn't get into my BoH to
get holy water to uncurse it. Damn! Well, I hadn't prayed for a long
time... it worked. Mjollnir got uncursed, and I managed to bless my
Boh. By now I was getting fed up of all these priests, so, seeing as I
had plenty charges in my wands of Wishing, I wished up a ring of
conflict, and let them take care of each other. I slipped past Famine,
found the altar, and ...


